In .NET 10 (and late .NET 9), Android's `adjustResize` mode was fully replaced by the **WindowInsets / edge-to-edge** model. `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` no longer triggers a layout resize.

## Recommended fix

**1. Use the built-in `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll`** (enabled by default in .NET 9+). It automatically scrolls the focused input into view. If you previously disabled it, re-enable it:

```csharp
// In MauiProgram.cs or on the page
Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Connect(handler);
```

**2. If you need manual control** (e.g., a pinned bottom bar), handle insets explicitly in your Android platform code:

```csharp
// Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
}

private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        // imeInsets.Bottom = keyboard height in px
        v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, imeInsets.Bottom);
        return insets;
    }
}
```

**3. Quick XAML-only workaround** — wrap your page content in a `ScrollView` so the auto-manager can scroll the input into view:

```xml
<ScrollView>
    <Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
        <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ... />
        <Entry Grid.Row="1" Placeholder="Type a message" />
    </Grid>
</ScrollView>
```

## TL;DR

| Approach | When to use |
|----------|-------------|
| `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (default) | Works for most inputs inside a scrollable layout |
| `WindowInsets` listener | Pinned bottom bars that must resize the layout |
| `ScrollView` wrapper | Quick fix if auto-scroll isn't triggering |

Remove any old `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` calls — they're no-ops now and can mask the real solution.
